==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|ballista||a military siege engine for throwing stones}} {{suffix|en||ic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈlɪs.tɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ballistic.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪstɪk|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Of or relating to [[ballistics]].
# {{lb|en|comparable}} Of or relating to [[projectile]]s moving under their own [[momentum]], air drag, [[gravity]] and sometimes [[rocket]] power.
# {{lb|en|comparable|slang}} Very [[angry]].
#: {{ux|en|When he heard him lie about it, he [[go ballistic|went '''ballistic''']].}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|ballistical}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|antiballistic}}
* {{l|en|guided}}, {{l|en|projectile}}

